<main class="wrap">
  <div class="article-head">
    <h1>About this site</h1>
  </div>

  <article>
    <p>I'm a software engineer, and this is where I write down the things I'd otherwise forget by the next time I need them — tool setups, workflow decisions, the fix for a problem that took an hour longer to find than it should have.</p>
    <p>Nothing here is theoretical. Every post comes from something that came up in actual working days: a setting worth changing, a command worth knowing, a debate worth ending with a rule instead of relitigating every time it comes up.</p>

    <div class="grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>What you'll find here</h3>
        <p>Practical, tested notes on tools and workflows — editors, version control, containers, and the small decisions that make a working day smoother.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>What you won't</h3>
        <p>No trend-chasing, no "10x engineer" claims, no content written to rank rather than to be useful.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>Have a correction, a request, or a topic you'd like covered? <a href="/contact.html">Reach out here</a>.</p>
  </article>
</main>
